#basePath	Day1

:: OpeningCutscene
@trigger SceneReady
@cutscene
@who    IntroCutscene

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(SpectrometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling", 1)
$call IntroCutscene->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(2)
$call TelescopeLook(155, -30)

:: ArrivalAtTheShed
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "IntroCutscene"
@cutscene
@who    Radio

$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling-Piano", 1)

$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven. Elijah, do you copy?\
Please log in and provide status update. 

$call Wait(2)

{@Astrid} Hi—um, this is Astrid, Elijah’s ... friend. Elijah doesn't seem to be here.\
Hello?\
Ugh. They can’t hear me.

{@Radio} Station Seven, please log in and report.

$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} I can’t, I don’t know how ...

$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} I told you, he's not there... Astrid? Is that you? $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_1]

{@Astrid} (*gasp*) Dad! I can’t believe it's you.
Are you still at the South Pole? Are you okay?
$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} Until I can get you clearance, this is a one-way radio. So I can't hear you...\
I’m sorry, Astrid . . . I wish I could’ve warned you in time.\
Elijah’s not there. He probably won’t be back for a while. When I saw his station come online. I assumed it was you.\
And if it really is you... Happy Birthday kiddo. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_2]

{@Astrid} What? Why not? Where is he?
Ugh, forgot . . . you can’t hear me. 

{@Dad} But.. in the mean time, my team here at IceCube have been working on rebuilding our knowledge of the cosmos.  $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_3]
What we lost during the collapse.. But then Elijah reached out to us. He’s onto something big...

{@Astrid} Onto what??

{@Dad} I'm so glad you're there though. We could really use your help. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_4]

{@Astrid} Because I know how any of this stuff works...

{@Dad} You don’t have clearance to most of the equipment, but that will come in time, first you need to submit data the old fashioned way. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_5]
{@Dad} Sending you the data now... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_6]

$call Wait(1)

$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(4.0)

{@Dad} OK, looks like you received the coordinates. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_7] 
{@Dad} See if you can move your telescope. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_8]

$call StartMonitorControls()
$call SetInputState(true)
$call StopMusic(2)
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("TelescopeControls", 0.4)
$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = false
$goto .MoveTelescopeReminder

:: MoveTelescopeReminder
$call Wait(10)
$if !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
    {@Dad} See if you can move your telescope. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_8(1)]
    $goto .MoveTelescopeReminder
$endif
// //TODO Shake UI hint

:: MoveYourTelescope
@trigger    OnTelescopeMoved
@when   !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = true
$call HintModals->Hide("TelescopeControls", 0.2)
Awesome, your equipment seems to be working.\
See those three dots above your monitor? Feel up for a game of hot an cold? $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s3]
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("NeutrinoNav", 0.4)

:: DadHotColdEncouragement1
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Nice! Getting warmer... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s4]
$call Wait(3)
{@Astrid} Remember when I was little and you used to make me find my easter basket this way?

:: DadHotColdEncouragement2
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Dad} Waaaaarrrrrmmmmmmeeerrrr! $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s6]

:: DadColder1
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavColder
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Dad} Getting Colder... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s5]

:: DadColder2
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavColder
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Colder...

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call HintModals->Hide("NeutrinoNav", 0.2)
{@Dad} Nice Job!\
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StartOpenMode()
{@Dad} Early this morning, Ice Cube detected a high energy neutrino coming from one of several possible stars in this location.\
You’ll see each of them highlighted on your display.\
Identifying these stars will be a great way for you get your feet wet and upgrade your system. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s7]
$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()

{@Dad} Alight. Select a possible neutrino origin on your display. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s8]
$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = true

$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("SelectStar", 0.4)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: OnStarSelected
@trigger    OnStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@cutscene
@interrupt

{@Dad} Oops.
It doesn't look like that is a possible neutrino origin.
Look for objects with a blue highlight.

:: OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@trigger    OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = false
$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = true
$call HintModals->Hide("SelectStar", 0.2)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)
{@Dad} Great! See if you can find Elijah’s operator manual. It's small, spiral bound... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s9]
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: OnRefGuideOpened
@trigger    OnRefGuideOpened
@when   temp:waitingForManualOpen
@boostScore 200
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = false
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Dad} Do you see your photometer in the equipment stack? That should tell you what the apparent magnitude of the star is.\
All you need to do is find that number in your reference guide and submit the data. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s11]
$call SetInputState(true)
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Dad} Hmmm, you might want to stay on target Little Bear. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s10]

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask2
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Dad} Looks like you’re drifting away from the cluster Astrid. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s17]

:: IncorrectSubmission
@trigger    OnIncorrectOpenIdSubmission

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)
{@Dad} Hmm, that wasn’t correct, remember to look at your photometer, and then line it up with the closest range in your manual. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s13]
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: DupliacteSubmission
@trigger    OnDuplicateOpenIdSubmission

{@Dad} Looks like you’ve already submitted that info.\
You won’t get any science points for identifying that property again. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s14]

:: FirstPoint
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 0
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
See if you can determine the apparent magnitude of the other stars in this cluster. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s15]

:: AnothaPoint
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 1
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

Great Job! go for another one. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s18]

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)
$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
{@Dad} Looks like you’ve identified enough stars to earn a higher clearance level. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s19]
You’ll need to tune to the right frequency on your radio to unlock your equipment. Tune to 375mHz. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s34]

$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("RadioControls", 0.4) 

$call Wait(1)

$call HintModals->Hide("RadioControls", 0.2)

//TODO Seperate Node Here
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 2.\ 
You are now cleared to use the color meter.\
Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.

{@Astrid} Riviting...

{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories.\
Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow.

$call Wait(2)
{@Astrid} Huh...
$call Wait(2)

{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction...
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Awesome, your rig is upgraded! Up for another game of hot and cold?\
This time I need you to find the constellation Perseus. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s20] 

{@Astrid} Perseus, huh?

$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: DadHotColdEncouragement3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Getting waarrmer... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s21]

:: DadHotColdEncouragement4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Dad} Waaaaarrrrrmmmmmmeeerrrr! $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s23]

:: DadColder3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Dad} Getting Colder... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s22] 

:: DadColder4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Dad} Colder...

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)
$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)
$call StartPuzzleMode()
{@Astrid} Whoooaa... what's that?

$call Wait(1)
{@Dad} Alright kiddo, this was the... important thing I was telling you about earlier.\
On your screen is all known information about the stars in Persius.\
You just need to logic your way through it and input data from your equipment into the grid.\ 
I’ll help you get started. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s24]
{@Dad} Select the star that matches the only location listen on your grid.\
You’ll see locations in your celestial compass. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s25]
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("FirstPuzzleStar", 0.4)
$call SetInputState(true)
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$set temp:waitingForSelectAtik = true

:: FirstPuzzleStarSelected
@trigger   OnStarSelected
@when   starName = "Atik", temp:waitingForSelectAtik
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForSelectAtik = false
$call HintModals->Hide("FirstPuzzleStar", 0.2)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)
Great, we can use our color meter and photometer to fill in data for Atik, select the Apparent Magnintude space in the puzzle grid. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s26]
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: PerseusPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Perseus"
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Dad}  Excellent! $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s31]
Gosh it’s late where you’re at.. Get some rest kiddo.\
We’ll try to figure out 2 way communication tomorrow... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s33]

{@Astrid} (*yawns*) That's about the only thing you've said that's made any sense...
$call Wait(1)
$call LoadNextDay()